---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getSpecIndex } from "../lib/specs.ts";

const specs = getSpecIndex();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How this site was built — Andrius Riauba"
  description="How riauba.org is built: a spec-to-deploy AI delivery pipeline, with every spec, its status and its merged pull request."
  path="/how-this-site-was-built"
>
  <h1>How this site was built</h1>

  <p>
    This site is built from a written specification for each feature, not from
    an open-ended conversation. Every change follows the same pipeline: a short
    spec describing the goal and its acceptance criteria, a plan mapping each
    acceptance criterion to tests, test-first implementation, an independent
    test pass, a code review, and a documentation update — in that order, for
    every spec.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two steps require a human to explicitly approve before anything moves
    forward. First, the plan itself: before any code is written, Andrius reviews
    and approves the implementation plan (or sends it back with amendments).
    Second, the pull request: every spec lands as its own PR, reviewed before
    merge, and nothing deploys automatically from a merge — production deploys
    are a separate, manual, one-click step. Nothing ships without both of those
    gates.
  </p>

  <p>
    Each spec's full history — every phase, how many iterations it took, and any
    bugs found along the way — is recorded in its own ship log under{" "}
    <code>docs/specs/</code>. The table below lists every spec in that
    directory, in order, with a link to its merged pull request where one
    exists.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Spec</th>
        <th>Title</th>
        <th>Status</th>
        <th>PR</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {specs.map((spec) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{String(spec.number).padStart(3, "0")}</td>
          <td>{spec.title}</td>
          <td>{spec.status}</td>
          <td>{spec.pr && <a href={spec.pr}>PR</a>}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</BaseLayout>
